#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:138
msgid ""
"The time that this slide remains visible before the slideshow attempts to "
"change to the next slide. In other words, it’s the animation timeline’s "
"length. Leave this option empty to let LayerSlider manage it automatically. "
"This value is in milliseconds, so the value 1000 means 1 second."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:153
msgid ""
"This option controls the stacking order of layers that overlap. In CSS, it’s "
"commonly called as z-index. Elements with a higher value are stacked in "
"front of elements with a lower one, effectively covering them. By default, "
"this value is calculated automatically based on the order of your layers. "
"Simply re-ordering them in the layers list can fix overlap issues. Use this "
"option only if you want to set your own value manually in special cases like "
"using static layers."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:155
msgid ""
"On each slide, the stacking order starts counting from 100. Providing a "
"number less than 100 will put the layer behind every other layer on all "
"slides. Specifying a much greater number like 500 will make the layer to be "
"on top of everything else."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:159
msgid ""
"Sets the desired behavior when content does not fit into the layer.<br><br>\n"
"\n"
"\t\t<b>Visible:</b> Overflowing content will be visible, which is the "
"default behavior in most cases. <br><br>\n"
"\n"
"\t\t<b>Hidden:</b> Overflowing content will be clipped, and will not be "
"visible. <br><br>\n"
"\n"
"\t\t<b>Auto:</b> Makes the layer scrollable when it has overflowing content."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:169
msgid ""
"Controls whether users can select text and other interface elements of this "
"layer. <br><br>\n"
"\n"
"\t\t<b>Inherit</b> uses the global value set in Project Settings → "
"Miscellaneous."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:176
msgid ""
"The minimum responsive ratio specifies the smallest size your layers can "
"shrink to when viewed on smaller screens. By default, this value is zero, "
"and there’s no size limitation. The value 1 corresponds to the layer’s "
"original size, making it impossible to become smaller."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:181
msgid ""
"The maximum responsive ratio specifies the largest size your layers can "
"enlarge to when viewed on bigger screens. There’s no size limitation by "
"default. The value 1 corresponds to the layer’s original size, making it "
"impossible to become larger. The value 2 means the layer can double in its "
"size."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:210
msgid ""
"Shifts the layer position from its original with the given amount on the "
"selected axis. Refer to the below options to see special values and "
"supported units."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:233
msgid ""
"Shifts the layer starting position with the given amount on the selected "
"axis. Layers animate from the offset value toward their position set under "
"the <b>STYLE</b> menu. Refer to the below options to see special values and "
"supported units."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:255
msgid ""
"Shifts each text fragment starting position with the given amount on the "
"selected axis. Text fragments animate from the offset value toward the whole "
"joint text. Refer to the below options to see special values and supported "
"units."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:278
msgid ""
"Shifts the layer position with the given amount while it’s animating out. "
"Layers animate from their current state toward the value you set here. Refer "
"to the below options to see special values and supported units."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:301
msgid ""
"Shifts each text fragment position with the given amount on the selected "
"axis while the layer animates out. Text fragments animate from the whole "
"joint text toward the value you set here. Refer to the below options to see "
"special values and supported units."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:313
msgid ""
"Shifts the layer position with the given amount of intensity on the X axis "
"by scrolling up or down on your site."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:315
#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:329
#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:466
#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:480
#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:602
#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:617
#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:632
#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:749
#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:764
#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:777
msgid ""
"You can use decimal values and go over the pre-defined ranges to fine-tune "
"the animation intensity."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:327
msgid ""
"Shifts the layer position with the given amount of intensity on the Y axis "
"by scrolling up or down on your site."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:355
msgid ""
"Scales the layer with the given amount on the selected axis. Use the value 1 "
"for the original size. The value 2 will double, while 0.5 will shrink the "
"layer to half of its original size. A negative value flips the layer on the "
"given axis."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:379
msgid ""
"Sets the initial layer scale on the selected axis before the layer starts "
"animating in. Use the value 1 for the original size. The value 2 will "
"double, while 0.5 will shrink the layer to half of its original size. A "
"negative value flips the layer on the given axis. Layers animate from this "
"value toward their appearance set under the <b>STYLE</b> menu."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:403
msgid ""
"Sets the initial scale of each text fragment on the selected axis before "
"they start animating in. Use the value 1 for the original size. The value 2 "
"will double, while 0.5 will shrink text fragments to half of their original "
"size. A negative value flips text fragments on the given axis. Text "
"fragments animate from this value toward the whole joint text. Refer to the "
"below options to see special values and supported units."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:427
msgid ""
"Scales the layer with the given amount on the selected axis while it’s "
"animating out. Use the value 1 for the original size. The value 2 will "
"double, while 0.5 will shrink the layer to half of its original size. A "
"negative value flips the layer on the given axis. Layers animate from their "
"current state toward the value you set here."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:451
msgid ""
"Scales each text fragment with the given amount on the selected axis while "
"they’re animating out. Use the value 1 for the original size. The value 2 "
"will double, while 0.5 will shrink each fragment to half of its original "
"size. A negative value flips the fragments on the given axis. Text fragments "
"animate from the whole joint text toward the value you set here."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:464
msgid ""
"Scales the layer with the given amount of intensity on the X axis by "
"scrolling up or down on your site."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:478
msgid ""
"Scales the layer position with the given amount of intensity on the Y axis "
"by scrolling up or down on your site."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:503
msgid ""
"Rotates the layer by the given number of degrees on the selected axis. "
"Negative values are allowed for counterclockwise rotation."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:524
msgid ""
"Sets the initial layer rotation by the given number of degrees on the "
"selected axis before the layer starts animating in. Negative values are "
"allowed for counterclockwise rotation. Layers animate from this value toward "
"their appearance set under the <b>STYLE</b> menu."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:545
msgid ""
"Sets initial rotation of each text fragment by the given number of degrees "
"on the selected axis before they start animating in. Negative values are "
"allowed for counterclockwise rotation. Text fragments animate from this "
"value toward the whole joint text."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:566
msgid ""
"Rotates the layer with the given number of degrees on the selected axis "
"while it’s animating out. Negative values are allowed for counterclockwise "
"rotation. Layers animate from their current state toward the value you set "
"here."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:587
msgid ""
"Rotates each text fragment with the given number of degrees on the selected "
"axis while they’re animating out. Negative values are allowed for "
"counterclockwise rotation. Text fragments animate from the whole joint text "
"toward the value you set here."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:600
msgid ""
"Rotates the layer with the given amount of intensity by scrolling up or down "
"on your site."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:615
msgid ""
"Rotates the layer with the given amount of intensity on the X axis by "
"scrolling up or down on your site."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:630
msgid ""
"Rotates the layer with the given amount of intensity on the Y axis by "
"scrolling up or down on your site."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:654
msgid ""
"Skews the layer by the given number of degrees on the selected axis. "
"Negative values are allowed for the reverse direction."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:674
msgid ""
"Sets the initial layer skew on the selected axis before the layer starts "
"animating in. Negative values are allowed for the reverse direction. Layers "
"animate from this value toward their appearance set under the <b>STYLE</b> "
"menu."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:694
msgid ""
"Sets the initial skew of each text fragment on the selected axis before they "
"start animating in. Negative values are allowed for the reverse direction. "
"Text fragments animate from this value toward the whole joint text."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:714
msgid ""
"Skews the layer with the given amount of degrees on the selected axis while "
"it’s animating out. Negative values are allowed for the reverse direction. "
"Layers animate from their current state toward the value you set here."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:734
msgid ""
"Skews each text fragment with the given amount of degrees on the selected "
"axis while they’re animating out. Negative values are allowed for the "
"reverse direction. Text fragments animate from the whole joint text toward "
"the value you set here."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:747
msgid ""
"Skews the layer with the given amount of intensity on the X axis by "
"scrolling up or down on your site."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:762
msgid ""
"Skews the layer with the given amount of intensity on the Y axis by "
"scrolling up or down on your site."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:775
msgid ""
"Changes the transparency of the layer with the given amount of intensity by "
"scrolling up or down on your site."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:781
msgid ""
"The length of the scroll transition in milliseconds. A second equals to 1000 "
"milliseconds. <br><br> Using smaller values will result in quick and fast "
"animations, while larger values will result in slower and delayed animations."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:785
msgid ""
"Choose a center point for scroll transition layers where they will be "
"aligned perfectly according to their original position. <br><br> <b>Inherit</"
"b>: Uses the global value set in Project Settings → Defaults. <br><br> "
"<b>Top</b>: When the top edge of the slider is at the top of the viewport. "
"<br><br> <b>Center</b>: When the center of the slider is at the center of "
"the viewport. <br><br> <b>Bottom</b>: When the bottom edge of the slider is "
"at the bottom of the viewport."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:789
msgid ""
"Choose whether Scroll Transition should watch for the project position or "
"the scene progression. By default, Scroll Transition won’t animate while the "
"project is pinned when using a Sticky or Scroll Scene. Choose the “Scene” "
"option if you’d like to use them in combination."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:817
#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:840
msgid ""
"The transform origin is the point around which transformations are applied. "
"For example, a layer may rotate around its center point or an entirely "
"custom point like one of its corners. See the below options for common "
"values."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:842
msgid ""
"This transform origin takes effect when you scroll past the center point set "
"for this layer in Scroll Transition Properties."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:859
msgid ""
"Changes the perspective of animated objects in the 3D space. Large values of "
"perspective cause milder transformations. Smaller values cause stronger and "
"more noticeable transformations."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:864
msgid ""
"Mirrors the selected transition properties on slide change based on whether "
"you navigate forward or backward in the slider. For example, if a layer "
"normally animates from left to right, it’ll go the opposite direction from "
"the right to the left when you navigate backward."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:889
msgid ""
"Clips (cuts off) the sides of layers by the given amount specified in pixels "
"or percentages. Similar to animating layer dimensions, except it will not "
"shift the layer and its contents. The four values are in order: top, right, "
"bottom, and the layer’s left side. A four-point polygonal cutout can also be "
"used by providing 4 pairs of coordinates, separated by commas. Refer to the "
"provided examples for acceptable values."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:914
msgid ""
"Clips (cuts off) the sides of each text fragment by the given amount "
"specified in pixels or percentages. The four values are in order: top, "
"right, bottom, and left. A four-point polygonal cutout can also be used by "
"providing 4 pairs of coordinates, separated by commas. Refer to the provided "
"examples for acceptable values."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:921
msgid ""
"Clips (cuts out) a polygonal shape from the layer by the given amount "
"specified in pixels or percentages. LayerSlider currently supports polygons "
"with 4 points, and it can be used by providing 4 pairs of coordinates "
"separated by commas. Refer to the provided examples for acceptable values."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:946
msgid ""
"The timing function of the animation. With this function, you can manipulate "
"the movement of the animated object. Please click on the link to open <a "
"href=\"https://easings.net/\" target=\"_blank\">easings.net</a> for more "
"information and more detailed examples."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:952
msgid ""
"The width of the layer in pixels or percents. Percentage values are relative "
"to the project canvas size."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:962
msgid ""
"Sets the layer’s initial width before it starts animating in. Layers animate "
"from this value toward their appearance set under the <b>STYLE</b> menu. You "
"can use pixels or percents. Percentage values are relative to the project "
"canvas size."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:972
msgid ""
"Changes the layer’s width while it’s animating out. Layers animate from "
"their current state toward the value you set here. You can use pixels or "
"percents. Percentage values are relative to the project canvas size."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:977
msgid ""
"The height of the layer in pixels or percents. Percentage values are "
"relative to the project canvas size."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:987
msgid ""
"Sets the layer’s initial height before it starts animating in. Layers "
"animate from this value toward their appearance set under the <b>STYLE</b> "
"menu. You can use pixels or percents. Percentage values are relative to the "
"project canvas size."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:997
msgid ""
"Changes the layer’s height while it’s animating out. Layers animate from "
"their current state toward the value you set here. You can use pixels or "
"percents. Percentage values are relative to the project canvas size."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1002
msgid ""
"The layer’s position from the left edge of the project canvas. You can use "
"pixels and percents. Percentage values align the layer’s center point to the "
"given position, so 50% places the layer exactly at the center. The 0% and "
"100% special values align the layer to the left and right edges."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1007
msgid ""
"The layer’s position from the top edge of the project canvas. You can use "
"pixels and percents. Percentage values align the layer’s center point to the "
"given position, so 50% places the layer exactly at the middle. The 0% and "
"100% special values align the layer to the top and bottom edges."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1011
msgid ""
"Useful when you want to position layers relative to the right side. In this "
"case, set the value of the left position to 100% and enter the distance from "
"the right side in this field as a negative value in pixels."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1015
msgid ""
"The layer’s minimum width. Setting a value prevents the layer from becoming "
"smaller than specified. Supported units: <br><br> <b>px:</b> A fixed value "
"specified in pixels. <br><br> <b>%:</b> Percentage of the entire project "
"width. <br><br> <b>em:</b> Relative to the layer’s font size. If the layer’s "
"font size is 36px, 1em will translate into exactly 36 pixels, while 1.5em "
"will be 54px. <br><br> <b>rem:</b> The same as <b>em</b>, but it’s relative "
"to the global font size set on the &lt;html&gt; root element."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1019
msgid ""
"The layer’s minimum height. Setting a value prevents the layer from becoming "
"smaller than specified. Supported units: <br><br> <b>px:</b> A fixed value "
"specified in pixels. <br><br> <b>%:</b> Percentage of the entire project "
"height. <br><br> <b>em:</b> Relative to the layer’s font size. If the "
"layer’s font size is 36px, 1em will translate into exactly 36 pixels, while "
"1.5em will be 54px. <br><br> <b>rem:</b> The same as <b>em</b>, but it’s "
"relative to the global font size set on the &lt;html&gt; root element."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1023
msgid ""
"The layer’s maximum width. Setting a value prevents the layer from becoming "
"larger than specified. Supported units: <br><br> <b>px:</b> A fixed value "
"specified in pixels. <br><br> <b>%:</b> Percentage of the entire project "
"width. <br><br> <b>em:</b> Relative to the layer’s font size. If the layer’s "
"font size is 36px, 1em will translate into exactly 36 pixels, while 1.5em "
"will be 54px. <br><br> <b>rem:</b> The same as <b>em</b>, but it’s relative "
"to the global font size set on the &lt;html&gt; root element."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1027
msgid ""
"The layer’s maximum height. Setting a value prevents the layer from becoming "
"larger than specified. Supported units: <br><br> <b>px:</b> A fixed value "
"specified in pixels. <br><br> <b>%:</b> Percentage of the entire project "
"height. <br><br> <b>em:</b> Relative to the layer’s font size. If the "
"layer’s font size is 36px, 1em will translate into exactly 36 pixels, while "
"1.5em will be 54px. <br><br> <b>rem:</b> The same as <b>em</b>, but it’s "
"relative to the global font size set on the &lt;html&gt; root element."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1032
msgid ""
"Useful when you want to position layers relative to the bottom. In this "
"case, set the value of the top position to 100% and enter the distance from "
"the bottom edge in this field as a negative value in pixels."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1037
msgid ""
"The length of the transition in milliseconds. A second equals to 1000 "
"milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1041
msgid ""
"The length of the transition in milliseconds. A second is 1000 milliseconds. "
"Supports special - randomized or cycled - values. Special values are chosen "
"at every step/repeat start."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1047
msgid ""
"Delays the transition of each text fragment relative to each other. A second "
"equals to 1000 milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1051
msgid ""
"Determines what triggers the parallax effect. <br><br>\n"
"<b>Cursor</b>: Reacts to mouse movement. <br><br>\n"
"<b>Scroll</b>: The parallax effect is triggered by scrolling on your site. "
"<br><br>\n"
"<b>Automated</b>: Simulates a continuous mouse movement along a predefined "
"path, such as a circle or triangle. <br><br>\n"
"<b>Random</b>: Simulates random mouse movements within a specified area."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1059
msgid ""
"Defines layer movement. <br><br>\n"
"<b>2D</b>: Layers shift horizontally and/or vertically.<br><br>\n"
"<b>3D</b>: Layers shift horizontally and/or vertically, and also tilt/rotate "
"in 3D space."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1065
msgid ""
"Specifies which axes influence layer movement (and rotation when using 3D), "
"restricting motion to horizontal, vertical, both, or none."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1069
msgid ""
"Sets the intensity of the parallax effect. Use negative values to shift "
"layers in the opposite direction."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1074
msgid ""
"Controls how quickly layers move into position when the mouse first enters "
"the slider area.<br><br> If you set a low or zero Move Duration, layers "
"would normally react instantly to the cursor’s position. With Enter "
"Duration, you can create a smoother entry by defining a separate timing for "
"this initial movement, after which the regular Move Duration will take "
"effect."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1078
msgid ""
"Controls the speed of layer movement. This value is in milliseconds (1 "
"second = 1000 milliseconds)."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1082
msgid ""
"Controls the speed of layer movement. This value is in milliseconds (1 "
"second = 1000 milliseconds). Supports randomized values."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1086
msgid ""
"Controls how quickly layers return to their original position when the mouse "
"cursor leaves the slider area and the Reset option is enabled. This value is "
"in milliseconds (1 second = 1000 milliseconds)."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1091
msgid ""
"Controls the intensity of layer movement (and rotation when using 3D). "
"Increase this value for more dramatic motion, or decrease it for a subtler "
"effect. Negative values are allowed."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1096
msgid ""
"Controls the intensity of layer tilt/rotation in 3D space. Increase this "
"value for more dramatic effect, or decrease it for a subtler one. Negative "
"values are allowed."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1100
msgid ""
"Sets the path for the automated parallax effect to follow, moving the layer "
"along the selected shape."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1104
msgid "Sets the movement direction along the selected path."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1108
msgid ""
"Defines a horizontal and vertical range that forms an area around the "
"slider’s center. The effect simulates random mouse cursor movements within "
"this area, with the layer’s parallax motion responding accordingly. <br><br> "
"This field must use LayerSlider’s random syntax to generate randomized "
"values. See the examples below for reference."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1112
#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1116
msgid ""
"Sets the start time of the selected transition with the given amount of "
"milliseconds. A second equals to 1000 milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1118
msgid ""
"This value overwrites the normal “Start at” value in the first cycle if the "
"layer is on the first slide."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1123
msgid ""
"The starting time of this transition. Choose from one of the pre-defined "
"options to use relative timing, which then can also be shifted with custom "
"operations below."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1126
msgid ""
"Shifts the above selected starting time by performing a custom operation."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1128
msgid ""
"For example, “- 1000” will advance the animation by playing it 1 second "
"(1000 milliseconds) earlier."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1132
msgid ""
"Opacity specifies the transparency of layers. You can enter a decimal number "
"between 0 and 1. The value 0 means the layer is fully transparent and "
"invisible, while the value 1 results in a fully solid and opaque layer."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1137
msgid ""
"Filters provide effects like blurring, color shifting, or changing the "
"brightness, contrast, saturation of your layers, among many others. Use the "
"below options to easily apply multiple filters."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1142
msgid ""
"Sets the initial layer filters before it starts animating in. Layers animate "
"from this value toward their appearance set under the <b>STYLE</b> menu. "
"Filters provide effects like blurring, color shifting, or changing the "
"brightness, contrast, saturation of your layers, among many others. Use the "
"below options to easily apply multiple filters on your layers."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1147
msgid ""
"Applies filters on the layer while it’s animating out. Layers animate from "
"their current state toward the value you set here. Filters provide effects "
"like blurring, color shifting, or changing the brightness, contrast, "
"saturation of your layers, among many others. Use the below options to "
"easily apply multiple filters on your layers."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1151
msgid ""
"Wait time between movements in milliseconds. A second is 1000 milliseconds. "
"Supports randomized values."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1155
msgid ""
"Wait time between repeats in milliseconds. A second is 1000 milliseconds. "
"Supports special - randomized or cycled - values. Special values are chosen "
"at every repeat start.<br><br>\n"
"\n"
"\t\t\t\tThis setting depends on the number of repeats. When using with Yoyo, "
"it applies to both the forward and backward (Yoyo) animations. If you only "
"want the wait time to occur after the Yoyo animation, use the Yoyo Wait "
"setting instead."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1161
msgid ""
"Yoyo Wait time between repeats in milliseconds. A second is 1000 "
"milliseconds. Supports special - randomized or cycled - values. Special "
"values are chosen at every Yoyo start.<br><br>\n"
"\n"
"\t\t\t\tIf you are using Repeat Wait with Yoyo but don’t want the repeat "
"wait time to apply after the Yoyo animation completes, enter a negative "
"value here. For example, if Repeat Wait is set to 1000ms, you can specify "
"-1000ms for this option."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1167
msgid ""
"Step Wait time between repeats in milliseconds. A second is 1000 "
"milliseconds. Supports special - randomized or cycled - values. Special "
"values are chosen at every step start.<br><br>\n"
"\n"
"\t\t\t\tThis setting is only available when using cycled values for "
"transition properties, and it only applies between steps. It will not be "
"applied after the final step.\n"
"\t\t"
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1174
msgid ""
"Layers can be kept at their place across multiple slides. Here you can "
"select the slide on which this layer should animate out."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1178
msgid ""
"By default, LayerSlider will start playing your project when it enters the "
"viewport so that visitors will not miss the animation and effects you "
"intended them to see, even if the project is below the fold. This behavior "
"is controlled by the Project Settings → Slideshow → Start Only In Viewport "
"option.<br><br>\n"
"\n"
"\t\tHowever, there are cases where you might want to display certain "
"interface elements immediately, even if the project canvas is only partially "
"visible and the playback of your project hasn’t started yet.<br><br>\n"
"\n"
"\t\tWith this option, you can exclude layers from waiting for the playback "
"to begin, and they will start the selected transitions immediately."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1191
msgid ""
"It looks like you’ve disabled Google Fonts in LayerSlider plugin settings. "
"We recommend enabling Google Fonts, so you can enhance your content with "
"beautiful and unique typography."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1194
msgid ""
"Enhance your content with beautiful and unique typography. Google Fonts "
"provides over a thousand web-optimized fonts."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1196
msgid "Browse Google Fonts"
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1219
msgid ""
"Sets the size of the background image. The image can be left to its natural "
"size, stretched, or constrained to fit the available space."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1223
msgid ""
"When enabled, the layer background will use the whole slide area, acting "
"like a slide background, but only the part covered by the layer will be "
"visible. It creates an effect as if you were looking through the layer - "
"like a window - to the background.\n"
"\t\t\t<br><br>\n"
"\n"
"\t\t\t<b>Continuous Background:</b><br>\n"
"\t\t\tThe cut out part is static and will not change as the layer moves.\n"
"\n"
"\t\t\t<br><br>\n"
"\n"
"\t\t\t<b>Dynamic for Transitions:</b><br>\n"
"\t\t\tThe cut out part is dynamic and will show the corresponding part of "
"the background for the selected transition type as the layer moves.\n"
"\n"
"\t\t\t<br><br>\n"
"\n"
"\t\t\tUseful tip: use this feature with more layers and the same background "
"to create great effects."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1239
msgid "Explore Live Examples"
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1263
msgid ""
"With this option, you can customize the easing of the Smart Background "
"animation for supported transition types, such as Loop and Parallax. By "
"adjusting the easing, you can control how smoothly or dynamically the "
"background content moves in relation to the layer. This gives you even more "
"flexibility to fine-tune the visual flow of your animations."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1265
msgid ""
"An easing is the timing function of the animation. With it, you can "
"manipulate the movement of the animated object. Please click on the link to "
"open <a href=\"https://easings.net/\" target=\"_blank\">easings.net</a> for "
"more information and more detailed examples."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1271
msgid ""
"A slide alias name, which you can use in your URLs with a hash tag so "
"LayerSlider will start with the corresponding slide when visitors arrive to "
"the page. <br><br> Example: domain.com/page/#welcome<br><br>Use only "
"lowercase alphanumeric values. You can also use this feature to implement "
"slide navigation with links."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1275
msgid ""
"The length of the scrollable area. Use larger values to keep the slider "
"visible for longer, and play animations slower in case of a Scroll Scene. "
"Supported units: <br><br> <b>px:</b> A fixed value specified in pixels. "
"<br><br> <b>%</b> or <b>sh:</b> Percentage of the slider height. 1sh equals "
"to 1% of the slider height. This value scales dynamically when the slider’s "
"size changes. <b> <br><br> vh:</b> Percentage of the viewport (browser "
"window) height. 1vh equals to 1% of the viewport height. This value scales "
"dynamically when the browser window is resized."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1279
msgid ""
"Creates empty space above and below your projects (i.e. margins). Supported "
"units: <br><br> <b>px:</b> A fixed value specified in pixels. <br><br> <b>%</"
"b> or <b>sh:</b> Percentage of the slider height. 1sh equals to 1% of the "
"slider height. This value scales dynamically when the slider’s size changes. "
"<b> <br><br> vh:</b> Percentage of the viewport (browser window) height. 1vh "
"equals to 1% of the viewport height. This value scales dynamically when the "
"browser window is resized."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1283
msgid ""
"Enter the slide number you want your project to start with, or choose from "
"the below options."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1287
msgid ""
"The minimum distance between the slider and viewport edges when Performance "
"Mode should activate as described on the right. Supported units: <br><br> "
"<b>px:</b> A fixed value specified in pixels. <br><br> <b>%</b> or <b>sh:</"
"b> Percentage of the slider height. 1sh equals to 1% of the slider height. "
"This value scales dynamically when the slider’s size changes. <b> <br><br> "
"vh:</b> Percentage of the viewport (browser window) height. 1vh equals to 1% "
"of the viewport height. This value scales dynamically when the browser "
"window is resized."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1293
msgid ""
"The scene position to animate to. Supported units: <br><br> <b>%:</b> "
"Percentage of the scene’s length. 0% means the beginning, while 100% means "
"the end of the scene. <br><br> <b>ms:</b> A specific point in time on the "
"scene’s animation timeline in milliseconds. A second is 1000 milliseconds. "
"Sticky scenes do not support this unit."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1297
msgid ""
"The timeline position to animate to or the amount to play forward/backward. "
"Supported units: <br><br> <b>%:</b> Percentage of the slide duration. 0% "
"means the beginning, while 100% means the end of the slide timeline. "
"<br><br> <b>ms:</b> A specific point or amount of time in milliseconds. A "
"second is 1000 milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1302
msgid ""
"Adjusts the width of the border in pixels. Larger values create a thicker, "
"more prominent border."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1306
msgid ""
"Specifies whether the border is drawn inside or outside the layer’s edges."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1310
msgid ""
"Determines whether the border animation plays sequentially around the "
"selected sides or all at once."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1314
msgid "Controls the border animation’s movement."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1318
msgid ""
"Sets how long the border animation takes from beginning to end in "
"milliseconds. A second equals to 1000 milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1319
msgid ""
"In Sequential mode, this time is divided among the selected sides, so each "
"side animates more quickly to fit within the overall length."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1323
msgid ""
"Sets how long to wait before the border animation begins, in milliseconds, "
"relative to the selected <b>START AT</b> option. A second equals to 1000 "
"milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1327
msgid "Sets the number of copies to generate from the original layer."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1331
msgid ""
"Delays each copy’s animation by a set number of milliseconds. This delay is "
"added on top of the previous one, so it accumulates for each additional "
"copy. One second equals 1000 milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1335
#, no-php-format
msgid ""
"Shifts each copy’s position horizontally by the specified amount, as if they "
"were created at an offset location from the original. The shift is "
"cumulative when using fixed values, so each copy is placed further from the "
"previous one. When using randomized values or expressions, however, each "
"copy is calculated independently and the shift is not cumulative. You can "
"use positive and negative values. Randomized values are also supported, but "
"avoid mixing units. Supported units: <ul><li><b>px:</b> A fixed value "
"specified in pixels.<br><br></li><li><b>sw:</b> Percentage of the slider "
"width. 1sw equals to 1% of the slider width. This value scales dynamically "
"when the slider’s size changes.<br><br></li><li><b>lw:</b> Percentage of the "
"layer width. 1lw equals to 1% of the layer width. This value scales "
"dynamically when the layer’s size changes.</li></ul>"
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1339
#, no-php-format
msgid ""
"Shifts each copy’s position vertically by the specified amount, as if they "
"were created at an offset location from the original. The shift is "
"cumulative when using fixed values, so each copy is placed further from the "
"previous one. When using randomized values or expressions, however, each "
"copy is calculated independently and the shift is not cumulative. You can "
"use positive and negative values. Randomized values are also supported, but "
"avoid mixing units. Supported units: <ul><li><b>px:</b> A fixed value "
"specified in pixels.<br><br></li><li><b>sh:</b> Percentage of the slider "
"height. 1sh equals to 1% of the slider height. This value scales dynamically "
"when the slider’s size changes.<br><br></li><li><b>lh:</b> Percentage of the "
"layer height. 1lh equals to 1% of the layer height. This value scales "
"dynamically when the layer’s size changes.</li></ul>"
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1343
msgid ""
"Defines the lower limit of the opacity applied across copies. By default, "
"copies gradually fade between the Max and Min values, and the distribution "
"is controlled by the Fade Method setting."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1347
msgid ""
"Defines the upper limit of the opacity applied across copies. By default, "
"copies gradually fade between the Max and Min values, and the distribution "
"is controlled by the Fade Method setting."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1351
msgid ""
"Determines how opacity values are distributed between the Max and Min "
"settings across copies. Different methods use various curves to define the "
"progression, creating either even or non-linear value sequences."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1355
msgid ""
"Adjusts the scale transformation for each additional copy by the specified "
"step value. Positive values progressively enlarge copies, while negative "
"values shrink them. When using random values, each copy will receive a "
"randomly chosen value from the defined range. When using cycle values, "
"copies will take the defined values in order, one after another."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1359
msgid ""
"Adjusts the rotation for each additional copy by the specified step value. "
"Positive values progressively rotate copies clockwise, while negative values "
"rotate them counterclockwise. When using random values, each copy will "
"receive a randomly chosen value from the defined range. When using cycle "
"values, copies will take the defined values in order, one after another."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1363
msgid ""
"Adjusts the width of each additional copy by the specified step value. "
"Positive values progressively increase the width, while negative values "
"decrease it."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1367
msgid ""
"Adjusts the height of each additional copy by the specified step value. "
"Positive values progressively increase the height, while negative values "
"decrease it."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1371
msgid ""
"Adjusts the parallax level of the Parallax Transition for each additional "
"copy by the specified step value. Positive values progressively increase the "
"parallax effect, while negative values decrease it."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1375
msgid ""
"Adjusts the movement duration of the Parallax Transition for each additional "
"copy by the specified step value. Positive values progressively increase the "
"duration, while negative values shorten it."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1379
msgid ""
"Sets how long to wait before the typing animation begins, in milliseconds, "
"relative to the selected <b>START AT</b> option. A second equals to 1000 "
"milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1383
msgid ""
"Sets the delay before the cursor gets hidden after the animation finishes, "
"in milliseconds. This only applies when Hide After Animation is enabled. A "
"second equals 1000 milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1387
msgid ""
"Sets the time for the mask to expand and fully cover the layer, in "
"milliseconds. A second equals 1000 milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1391
msgid ""
"Sets how long the mask stays fully covering the layer before collapsing, in "
"milliseconds. A second equals 1000 milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1395
msgid ""
"Sets the time for the mask to collapse and reveal the layer’s content, in "
"milliseconds. A second equals 1000 milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1399
msgid ""
"Sets the time offset between individual tiles when the selected animation "
"consists of multiple segments. This delay is cumulative, so each subsequent "
"tile starts later than the previous one by the specified amount. Measured in "
"milliseconds, where one second equals 1000 milliseconds."
msgstr ""

